1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:07,416
This is the Meridian IP-1 irrigation pump. This short video is about one solder joint on its main controller board.

2
00:00:08,866 --> 00:00:13,891
Inside the pump, the main controller board drives the motor, the valve and the sensors.

3
00:00:14,141 --> 00:00:19,909
The problem is at connector J1, the 24 V power input. Pin 2 is the ground pin.

4
00:00:21,359 --> 00:00:30,030
This is a cut through that hole. The board has four copper layers, and this pin is tied solidly to the ground copper on three of them.

5
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:37,012
In wave soldering, solder enters from the bottom. But the large copper areas pull heat out of the hole.

6
00:00:37,262 --> 00:00:43,599
The solder cools and freezes before it reaches the top. Here it fills only about 40% of the hole.

7
00:00:45,049 --> 00:00:51,270
The requirement for this product is IPC Class 3. Solder must fill at least 75% of the hole.

8
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:59,529
From the bottom, this joint looks normal, and the connector body hides the top. A visual check will not catch it.

9
00:00:59,779 --> 00:01:06,430
But the joint is weak. With vibration and heat it can crack, and the pump loses power.

10
00:01:07,880 --> 00:01:19,871
Here is what we need changed in the wave soldering process. 1: More preheat. The top side of the board at this connector should reach at least 110 °C before it touches the wave.

11
00:01:20,121 --> 00:01:26,145
2: Longer contact time. Slow the conveyor so this pin stays in the solder longer.

12
00:01:26,395 --> 00:01:32,059
3: Flux. Make sure flux gets all the way through the hole to the top side.

13
00:01:32,309 --> 00:01:37,833
With enough heat in the hole, the solder keeps flowing and fills the hole to the top.

14
00:01:39,283 --> 00:01:48,116
Please check this joint by X-ray, not by eye. Measure the fill height on J1 pin 2. It must be 75% or more.

15
00:01:48,367 --> 00:01:51,697
Send us the X-ray image with each lot.

16
00:01:53,147 --> 00:02:02,004
To summarize: more preheat, longer contact time, flux through the hole, and X-ray proof of 75% fill.

17
00:02:02,253 --> 00:02:09,322
On our side, the next board revision adds thermal relief on this pin, to make it easier to solder. Thank you.

